
The tee command reads input from stdin and writes it to a file while also displaying it on the terminal.

Think of it as:
Command → tee → Terminal
             ↘ File


cat file1 | tee file2 file3 file4 file5     --> to display & to copy file1 data to remaining all files at a time (override the data)


cat file1 | tee -a file2 file3 file4 file5    --> -a --> it won't override the existing data, it just append to existing data in remaining files
